cartridge "GRAPPLE/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' GRAPPLE - an original game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
' Phase 2: three cave maps of six varied galleries, bats and falling
' stalactites, hero animation, sound and a title tune.
' Phase 3: a side-view hero with a miner's helmet, a 4-frame walk cycle that
' turns into a run (1.5 px a frame after 0.4 s), facing his way (left poses
' mirrored into VRAM at start); a green exit arrow over the exit hole of the
' hero's gallery; a CAVE n card before each cave; HOW TO PLAY in 3 pages
' with the goal first; a clean GAME OVER panel (score, cave); stale sprite
' entries re-checked after hero jumps (never 5 on a line); 120 bytes of
' rope buffers moved to the RAM Amy keeps for its own sprite table (stack).
' Every gallery is proven passable by solver.mjs (reachability over the
' map and this hero physics, with timing windows) and replay.mjs (the
' solver's moves played on this ROM).
'
' A cave descent. The button fires a grappling hook; the stick aims it (up,
' up-left, up-right, left, right; no direction = up-forward). When the hook
' bites rock the rope tightens and the hero swings as a pendulum: LEFT/RIGHT
' pump the swing, UP/DOWN reel in/out, the button lets go and the hero flies
' with the swing's speed. Drop through the holes, gallery after gallery, to
' the cave passage at the bottom (cave clear; phase 5: was a pool of water). Spikes, bats and falling stalactites
' (they shake before they fall) cost a life, and so does the time bar.
' Catches in the air chain: each counted catch scores 10 x chain; a gem
' (phase 6: one a gallery, off the plain route) 100, 200 if grabbed in free
' flight; landing in a gallery deeper than ever this cave 200; the time
' left at the passage is a bonus (10 a second). Caves 1-3 use
' maps 1-3 (harder each: smaller holes and ledges, more and faster bats);
' from cave 4 the maps repeat with faster bats and less time.
'
' Screen: HUD row 1 (icons), cave rows 2-22, columns 2-29 (CRT safe area).
' Pattern and colour tables are shared by the three thirds (R4 = 0, R3 = $9F).
'   tiles 128..    scroll combos: (cell above, cell below) for 7 visual cell
'                  kinds (air, two rock textures, lit top edge, underside,
'                  spikes, water); rewritten from 8 pre-shifted copies when
'                  the scroll's pixel shift changes (the map's used ones)
'   PoolA, PoolB   rope tiles, two pools of 24 used on alternate frames
'   IcBase..       HUD and title icons
' The maps are stored as name rows: a map byte IS the combo tile of the cell
' (with the cell below); its collision kind is CollT[name].
' Sprites (16x16): the hero (2 layers, 10 poses), then by priority (phase
' 6) the score popup (its own entry, always shown: the others near it yield),
' the stalactites, bats, the flying hook, gems, the catch puff, a drip and
' the exit arrow, each added only if none of its 16 lines already has 4
' sprites (GpAdd: counts the accepted sprites overlapping it) -> never 5 on
' a line.
'
' Pendulum: theta 16 bits a turn; sin/cos from ROM tables only (SinT, AccT),
' no runtime trig and no multiply in the per-frame physics (one multiply
' per catch).
'
' Frame: Frame1 waits for the vertical blank, then GpBlit writes the sprite
' table, the combo tiles (if the shift changed), the rope tiles and names,
' the HUD; then the logic of the next frame runs.

const PassX = 200
const PassAY = 618
